  "ad6eec04-f34c-477c-8af5-7343e9e60188"],
 " (the default) all of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d98d15ad-0144-4c2f-af36-243058c1e789"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The shell of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " about ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], ":", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bad8109-b7b2-42d7-aa3c-831554877dc2"],
 " \[LongDash] the sphere of the graph metric, as a vertex ",
 StyleBox["set",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d51c90fb-f9d2-400f-89ab-fddd371fddd4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is the discrete analogue of a sphere, not of a circle: it is \
codimension-1 as a set, but on a lattice its vertices are pairwise \
non-adjacent, so it carries no cycle. The cyclic object is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraCircle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/FindInfraCircle", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9fddaf18-5a32-42f7-a391-bf9ba4fdab28"],
 ", which needs a thickened band for exactly that reason."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cbea3c0b-9814-4fe3-8245-3ae3f7a512c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The shell is the substrate of the volume-growth invariants. Its cardinality \
as a function of ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " is the surface-area profile, and on a flat lattice it grows ",
 StyleBox["linearly",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", which is the statement that the dimension is 2. The slope is a property \
of the tiling: 4 per step on the square grid, 3 on the hexagonal."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2319db95-a283-422b-9f98-66089e978da6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Option ",
 Cell[BoxData["Properties"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4de0f12c-f6e6-4524-8f3e-6e885dab9578"],
 " takes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1daaa80-480f-4aef-a68a-3d60df280dda"],
 " (default; the whole level set as one realisation), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "\"\<Separating\>\"", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b359f857-45ca-4f3b-9a3a-c0ece37b1775"],
 " (inclusion-minimal subsets separating the centre from beyond), or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Separating\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Connected\>\""}], "}"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6809e397-4f08-4deb-92ee-81c0c428e564"],
 ". Option ",
 Cell[BoxData["Method"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f97aca2-8115-4f06-b677-4275af71f54d"],
 " takes ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Exhaustive\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fbbb62f-670a-40b6-b01a-0aceae99967d"],
 " (default) or ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Greedy\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "86d8a912-28a8-4c6b-ae02-01d78b2fb592"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "\"\<Volume\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "026503e7-1716-470a-9175-945e5aef3df1"],
 " accessor gives the per-realisation vertex count as a list."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a3fee808-0ab7-45ba-96da-c05f8b2504a5"],

